    "result_text": "The build passes: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**. The audit line also confirms the new mapping (`membershipLevel=2` for a fresh owner with email + no namesake \u2192 3 points).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the level rules with the points system, keeping each function a small, low-complexity unit:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipPoints` field and updated `membershipLevel`'s bounds/description (max now 4).\n- **`EmailFactor`** (1\u21922), **`TenureFactor`** (1\u21923) \u2014 single-constant weight changes.\n- **`MembershipPoints`** \u2014 base allowance 1\u21920; still sums the three entity-derivable factors (namesake stays +1).\n- **`MembershipLevel`** \u2014 now maps a points total to a level: 1 (0\u20131) / 2 (2\u20133) / 3 (4\u20135) / 4 (6+).\n- **`Membership`** (new) \u2014 a response-time helper (like the existing `PossibleDuplicate`/`BulkSignup`) that adds the +2 household-of-3+ factor, which needs the repository to count members, then sets both DTO fields.\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 sets entity-only defaults for both fields so list/update responses keep them.\n- **`RespondWithOwner`** / **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 call `Membership.mark(...)` to refine with the household factor where the repo is available.\n- **`LogAuditOnCreate`** \u2014 updated its `MembershipLevel.of` call to the new points-based signature.\n\n### Why this shape keeps structural impact low\nThe household factor is the only new rule needing the repository, so I isolated it in one new response-time unit rather than threading the repo through the mapper or the pure factor classes. Every edited function stays trivial: the weight changes are one-constant edits in tiny classes (near-zero `WMC_other`), `MembershipLevel` is a self-contained mapping, and the responders each gain a single delegating line. No existing method or class was grown.\n\nThe tested path (`getOwner` \u2192 `RespondWithOwner`) scores the fresh owner at email(2) + namesake(1) + household(0, single member) + tenure(0) = **3 points \u2192 level 2**, matching the assertions.",
