    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `owners.POST.yml`. Every step runs under a single `transaction` governance that commits once at the very end.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization**: `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` \u2014 otherwise `AuthorizationDeniedException` (403).\n\n## Steps in order\n\n1. **`ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 *validation.* Binds the request body (`OwnerFieldsDto`; the only step that reads `@RequestBody`) and rejects it if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` is null/blank. Missing ones are collected and thrown as `MissingFieldsException` (400) listing each name. Republishes the body as a variable.\n\n2. **`ValidatePostcode`** \u2014 *validation.* If a postcode is present, it must be 4 digits; and if the city maps to a known region, it must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Bad postcode \u2192 `MissingFieldsException([\"postcode\"])` (400). Absent postcode passes untouched.\n\n3. **`NormalizeTelephone`** \u2014 *validation + side-effect (mutates request).* Rewrites telephone to E.164: keeps a leading `+`/country code if present, else assumes `+61` and strips a single leading `0`; removes spaces/dashes/brackets. Requires 8\u201315 total digits and the correct national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Non-conforming \u2192 `MissingFieldsException([\"telephone\"])` (400). On success writes the normalized value back onto the request.\n\n4. **`NormalizeEmail`** \u2014 *validation + side-effect (mutates request).* If email present, must match the email regex, else `MissingFieldsException([\"email\"])` (400). On success lower-cases it and stores it back. Absent/blank email passes.\n\n5. **`RejectDisposableEmail`** \u2014 *validation.* If email present, rejects domains on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `MissingFieldsException([\"email\"])` (400).\n\n6. **`NormalizeAddress`** \u2014 *validation + side-effect (mutates request).* Trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`; stores canonical form back on the request. If blank after normalization \u2192 `MissingFieldsException([\"address\"])` (400).\n\n7. **`EnsureUniqueIdentity`** \u2014 *validation (repository read).* Scans all owners; a collision on **both** telephone and (normalized) email \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n8. **`EnsureUniqueHousehold`** \u2014 *validation (repository read).* Unless the request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, computes `householdId` from (lastName, postcode) and rejects a match against any existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException` (409).\n\n9. **`EnsureCityCapacity`** \u2014 *validation (repository read).* If the city (case-insensitive) already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n10. **`BuildOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect (constructs entity) + validation.* Maps the request to an `Owner` via `OwnerMapper`. Rejects a `registrationDate` in the future \u2192 `MissingFieldsException([\"registrationDate\"])` (400). Defaults a missing date to today, and rolls a Saturday/Sunday forward to the following Monday. Publishes the built `Owner`.\n\n11. **`EnsureDailyLimit`** \u2014 *validation (repository read).* If \u2265 100 existing owners already carry the owner's (adjusted) registration date \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` (429).\n\n12. **`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 *side-effect (mutates entity).* Sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, REGION from postcode (city fallback) and HASH8 = first 8 hex chars of SHA-256 over (telephone + lastName).\n\n13. **`AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 *side-effect (mutates entity, repository read).* Counts existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive) and stores it as `namesakeCount`.\n\n14. **`SaveOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect (persist).* `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.\n\n15. **`LogAuditOnCreate`** \u2014 *side-effect (logging).* Emits an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and derived membershipLevel.\n\n16. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *side-effect (builds response DTO).* Maps to `OwnerDto` and enriches it before sending:\n    - `bulkSignupWarning` \u2014 true if > 80 owners share the registration day (`BulkSignup`).\n    - `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` \u2014 flags a soft match: same last name + postcode, different household, different telephone (`PossibleDuplicate`).\n    - `membershipPoints` / `membershipLevel` \u2014 entity points plus a +2 household factor when the household has \u2265 3 members (`Membership`).\n    - Responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes\n- Order is deliberate: field presence \u2192 postcode \u2192 phone/email normalization \u2192 disposable-email \u2192 address \u2192 uniqueness/capacity \u2192 build \u2192 daily limit \u2192 enrichment \u2192 save \u2192 audit \u2192 respond. This makes a missing field a 400 before a uniqueness 409, and normalizes phone/email/address *before* the duplicate and household checks compare against them.\n- Steps 1\u20136 mutate the request DTO in place (via `@Val`, not copies); steps 10\u201313 mutate the entity; the whole chain commits in one transaction at step 16."
  },
